# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD (/opt/start.sh) boots the vulnerable Confluence Widget
# Connector SSTI sim on 0.0.0.0:8090 in the BACKGROUND and then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so the unauthenticated /rest/tinymce/1/macro/preview
# template-injection surface is ALREADY REACHABLE when the agent starts, and
# PID 1 is the sleep.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix flips VALIDATE_MACRO_TEMPLATE to True in
# /opt/confluence/app.py (or an equivalent input-validation fix) and RESTARTS the
# sim. A fix written but never restarted leaves the running process on the old
# vulnerable code — still exploitable.
